n                                                                    <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/wordpress-course?utm_source=WsBlog&#038;utm_medium=blog_course_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\"\n                                       target=\"_blank\"\n                                       class=\"btn view-btn btn-sm\">\n                                        View Brochure\n                                    <\/a>\n                                \n                                <a target=\"_blank\"\n                                   href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/wordpress-course?utm_source=WsBlog&#038;utm_medium=blog_course_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\"\n                                   class=\"btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm\">\n                                    Learn More\n                                <\/a>\n                            <\/div>\n                        <\/div>\n                    <\/div>\n\n                \n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n    \n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What Does a Web Developer Do?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Web developers create and&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;websites and web applications, writing code that shapes both the appearance and the functionality for a seamless user experience.&nbsp;Almost every&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/social-media-platforms\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">social media platform<\/a>, e-commerce store, streaming service, and online application you use is built by a team of web developers.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Here is what their work typically involves:<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Building and designing websites and web applications using tools and programming languages such as&nbsp;PHP,&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/resources\/html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">HTML<\/a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/resources\/css\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">CSS<\/a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/resources\/python\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Python<\/a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/resources\/javascript\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">JavaScript<\/a>, and more.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Collaborating with designers, product managers, testers, and stakeholders to meet the client&#8217;s goals.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Turning designs into a fully functional product, while designers focus on the look and feel.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Handling ongoing maintenance and&nbsp;updates and&nbsp;fixing bugs that affect features or performance.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Improving speed, security, and scalability to keep the application running smoothly.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Types of Web Developers<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Before you get familiar with how to be a website developer, take a look at the different\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/types-of-web-development\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">types of developers<\/a>. Broadly, there are three primary types based on their area of expertise and specialization.<\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/web-developer-types.webp\" alt=\"Types of Web Developers\" class=\"wp-image-21376\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/web-developer-types.webp 2560w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/web-developer-types-300x169.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/web-developer-types-1024x576.webp 1024w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/web-developer-types-768x432.webp 768w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/web-developer-types-1536x864.webp 1536w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/web-developer-types-2048x1152.webp 2048w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">1. Front-End Developers<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Front-end developers work on the visual part of a&nbsp;website,&nbsp;the part users can view and interact with, such as colors, images, theme, fonts, and layout. They use three core languages,&nbsp;HTML, CSS, and&nbsp;JavaScript, to design web pages and make sure a site looks good and responds smoothly across all devices.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">2. Back-End Developers<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Back-end developers build the structure behind a website, handling everything users cannot see. Their work covers database storage, security, integrations, server management, and program logic, using server-side languages such as <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/resources\/java\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Java<\/a>, PHP, Python, <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/resources\/sql\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">SQL<\/a>, and React.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">3. Full-Stack Developers<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Full-stack developers&nbsp;handle both front-end and back-end work, building a complete website from its look and design to its core functionality. With experience, they gain command over the full range of tools and technologies needed to build an entire site.<\/p>\n\n\n\n        <div class=\"container position-relative mb-2\">\n            <div class=\"row pb-4\">\n                <h2 style=\"font-size:32px\">Upcoming Masterclass<\/h2>\n                <p>Attend our live classes led by experienced and desiccated instructors of Wscube Tech.<\/p>\n            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"owl-carousel myOwl\">\n            <div class=\"item\">\n                <a href=\"https:\/\/