scubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-web-developer\/#faq-question-1786340151331\",\"position\":1,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-web-developer\/#faq-question-1786340151331\",\"name\":\"1. What are the steps to\u00a0become\u00a0a web developer?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Start by learning the fundamentals like HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, then build core skills, take a structured course, and choose a specialization. After that, work on real projects, build a portfolio, and apply for jobs or freelance work.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-web-developer\/#faq-question-1786340162450\",\"position\":2,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-web-developer\/#faq-question-1786340162450\",\"name\":\"2. How long does it take to become a web developer?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"With consistent effort, most beginners become job-ready in about six to twelve months. The exact time depends on your learning pace, the hours you put in daily, and whether you follow a structured course or self-study.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-web-developer\/#faq-question-1786340175092\",\"position\":3,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-web-developer\/#faq-question-1786340175092\",\"name\":\"3. Can I become a web developer without a degree?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes, a formal degree is not mandatory. Many successful developers are self-taught or learn through a trusted web development course, and employers care more about your skills, projects, and portfolio than your qualifications.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-web-developer\/#faq-question-1786340188080\",\"position\":4,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-web-developer\/#faq-question-1786340188080\",\"name\":\"4. Which programming language should I learn first as a beginner?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Start with HTML and CSS, since they form the backbone of every website. Once you are comfortable, move on to JavaScript to add interactivity, and then explore <a href=\\\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/backend-languages\/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noreferrer noopener\\\">back-end languages<\/a> based on your chosen path.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-web-developer\/#faq-question-1786340200519\",\"position\":5,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-web-developer\/#faq-question-1786340200519\",\"name\":\"5. Do I need to be good at\u00a0maths\u00a0to become a web developer?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"No, web development relies more on logic and problem-solving than on advanced\u00a0maths. Basic arithmetic is enough for most front-end and back-end tasks, so weak\u00a0maths\u00a0skills should not hold you back.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-web-developer\/#faq-question-1786340217016\",\"position\":6,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-web-developer\/#faq-question-1786340217016\",\"name\":\"6. Can I learn web development on my own without a course?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes, self-learning is possible with free tutorials and practice. However, a structured course speeds up the process, keeps your learning organized, and adds credibility to your profile through certification.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-web-developer\/#faq-question-1786340224040\",\"position\":7,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-web-developer\/#faq-question-1786340224040\",\"name\":\"7. What skills do I need to become a web developer?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"You need technical skills like coding, responsive design, version control, and basic SEO, along with soft skills such as communication, problem-solving, and attention to detail to work well within a team.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-web-developer\/#faq-question-1786340240551\",\"position\":8,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-web-developer\/#faq-question-1786340240551\",\"name\":\"8. Should I choose front-end, back-end, or full-stack development?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Pick front-end if you enjoy design and visuals, back-end if you prefer logic and databases, and full-stack if you want to handle both. Beginners often start with front-end before expanding their skills.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-web-developer\/#faq-question-1786340253965\",\"position\":9,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-web-developer\/#faq-question-1786340253965\",\"name\":\"9. How important is a portfolio for getting a web developer job?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"A portfolio is very important, as it proves your skills through real projects.\u00a0Recruiters use it to judge your abilities, so include your best work along with the process and problems you solved.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage